# Privacy Policy — 7ème Prototype

*Last updated: 11/18/2026*

## In short

7ème Prototype collects no personal data. Everything you enter stays on
your device.

## Data we collect

None. The app has no user account, no server, no analytics, and no
advertising.

## Data stored on your device

Your items, sales, expenses, settings and photos are saved in a local
database inside the app's private folder. They are never transmitted. They
are removed if you uninstall the app, unless you exported them or your
phone included them in its own backup (iCloud on iOS, depending on your
settings).

## The only outgoing connection

When you scan a barcode, the app queries free public databases to try to
find the product name: Open Food Facts, Open Beauty Facts and Open Products
Facts.

Only the barcode is sent. No information about you, your device or your
inventory accompanies the request. If you are offline, the request fails
silently and you fill the form in by hand.

You can disable this lookup entirely: it is not required for the app to
work.

## Permissions requested

- **Camera**: read barcodes and photograph your items.
- **Photo library**: pick an existing photo to illustrate an item.

Photos are copied into the app's private folder and never leave it.

## Data sharing

No sharing, no selling, no transfer to third parties. Only you can export
your data, deliberately, through the backup feature.

## Your rights

Your data belongs to you and is under your sole control. You can export it,
restore it, or erase it entirely from the app's settings.

